# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Anton S. Bochkarev et al. (2024). Graph Atomic Cluster Expansion for Semilocal Interactions beyond Equivariant Message Passing.
#   Physical Review X. doi:10.1103/physrevx.14.021036  arXiv:2311.16326v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2311.16326v2 (sha256 efbf1fe3cbc5d93f...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 202 (Method/model). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/bochkarev2024.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: graph ACE (ACE(g), called GRACE in the registry; introduced
# here) and the ACE(g) fits whose errors are tabulated: the ten revised MD17
# molecules trained on 1,000 and on 50 configurations (Table I) and 3BPA
# (Table II). The four-atom Si cluster and carbon fits, and the carbon MACE
# model trained for comparison, have errors only in figures (Figs. 10, 11);
# their data sets and runs are encoded without results. Errors of other
# models quoted from the literature in Tables I and II are not encoded.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
