###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# Inference: about 2.3 ms per 3BPA molecule on an NVIDIA A100 for ACE(g)
# (recorded as inferenceHardware on the 3BPA 300 K result); for carbon, a
# 2,016-atom diamond supercell in LAMMPS on an A100 runs at 200 us/atom with
# ACE(g) and 400 us/atom with MACE, and the largest system that fits in
# 80 GB is 12,672 atoms for ACE(g) and 2,016 for MACE. The carbon timings
# have no tabulated accuracy result to sit on and are held in the encoding
# input. Training cost is not reported.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Introduces graph ACE: 'We extend the Atomic Cluster Expansion to incorporate graph basis functions' (Abstract; also Introduction). Recorded in the method registry as GRACE derived from ACE; the paper names it ACE(g) or grACE.
# - Si cluster and carbon errors are shown only in Figs. 10 and 11, so these fits (and the carbon MACE comparison model) have no BenchmarkResult.
# - Table I is captioned as revised MD17 while the text describes MD17 with 100,000 configurations per molecule; the results are linked to rMD17 in the encoding input. The DFT level of rMD17, 3BPA and the carbon data set is not stated in this paper.
# - The rMD17 energy errors are in meV per molecule (unit meV).
# - The architecture is described by graph types (dandelion (12224) for molecules, (12223) for carbon), which have no hyperparameter individual; nmax is 8 on the first layer and 32 on layer zero for the molecules.
# - The 3BPA errors are means over five models; the standard deviations of Table II are not encoded.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/bochkarev2024.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

